            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, if the paint is sound. Sealant bonds well to firmly adhered paint. Scrape away anything loose or peeling, clean off chalky residue with a damp rag and let it dry, and wipe with alcohol before caulking. If the paint is failing broadly, scrape and prime the trim first, then caulk, then repaint over the cured bead."
